  same function must reject (outside=1, bottom 629, rejected).
- F330 [Nit] FIX. The gate row `song_video_fullsize_short_portrait` at 390x400 requires the
  song video height above the 176 px (11 rem) cap, so a deleted orientation clause fails
  the row. Fail-first: one scratch gate run with the clause removed from the query read
  `video_height_px=176` (capped, width 99, ratio 563) and the row failed; with the clause
  the box is `video_height_px=300` at a 9:16 ratio. The clause behavior itself is
  unchanged.
- F350 [Nit] FIX. The `song.tsx` comment now states the real rule: a short desktop window
  is landscape, so the cap applies there too; only a portrait phone with a soft keyboard
  keeps the full-size box. The behavior is unchanged. The plan Turn 13 block holds a
  `Correction (turn 14, F350):` line instead of a history rewrite.
- No song picture or content file changed. No committed Red or adversarial assertion
